Workstream ID: omscs-specializations
Title: Compare six OMSCS specializations and persist an academic starter
Status: DONE
Milestone: Deliver the specialization ledger and shared academic basis with authorized publication
Dependencies: omscs-path-explorer, calm-interface, tracker-foundation
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/CareerOS/issues/15
Purpose: Show all six current online specialization requirement groups with
  subject rows, shared completion styling and grade-aware eligibility. Use
  the expressly authorized public academic starter consistently across
  saved course records, future recommendations, calendars and mission entry.
  Keep actual learning evidence and personal data outside that narrow
  authorized preset unchanged.

Tasks:
  [x] Confirm six-specialization scope and explicit public-default visibility.
  [x] Read all six official online specialization pages and degree grade rules.
  [x] Encode online-only groups, minimum sub-area counts and no double counting.
  [x] Add persistent starter initialization without overwriting explicit records.
  [x] Support catalogue-wide academic entries and grade-aware course reuse.
  [x] Add six compact specialization sections and completed-row green glow.
  [x] Align academic recommendations, calendars and mission/roadmap entry.
  [x] Preserve backups/journal, existing career data and isolated practice.
  [x] Qualify default/migration/conflict, allocation and responsive behavior.
  [x] Update focused documentation, evidence and same-identity tracking.
  [x] Correct next-course action alignment and divider spacing across widths.

Acceptance criteria:
  All six current OMSCS specializations have distinct labelled sections.
    Only explicitly online, current-catalogue subjects appear as requirement
    choices; published core/elective counts and category minima are respected.
  A shared recorded course appears completed everywhere it is shown. Green
    borders/glow indicate academic completion, not eligibility or mastery;
    grade/status text is accessible and reduced motion retains a steady cue.
  Degree-passing and specialization-eligible grades remain different. Courses
    below the specialization floor can use a free slot, never a required
    specialization slot or two slots simultaneously.
  The owner-authorized public starter is persisted and exported as academic
    data. Its centralized resume term drives future academic suggestions,
    calendars and mission/roadmap entry rather than page-local assumptions.
  Existing explicit records and custom choices are not silently replaced.
    Missing-profile initialization is distinct from an explicitly empty plan;
    conflicting/newer entries require a deliberate reviewed update.
  No academic seed or course grade completes learning checkpoints, evidence,
    recall, readiness, Atlas or timer activity. Practice uses fictional/empty
    academic data and cannot change the real starter or workspace.
  Normal pages remain concise and action-first; source detail is on demand.
    Frozen learning definitions and the approved README illustrations stay intact.
  Only values expressly approved for the public app preset are included in
    that product data. Do not copy other private input, actual grades/dates,
    transcripts or profile bodies into issues or shared continuity.
  Preserve live user previews and use disposable qualification contexts.
    Public-default consent alone is not commit, push or deployment authority;
    publication needs a separate owner decision and exact hosted evidence.

